### name: rel.distinct.numbers
--- source
LIST(1, 2, 2, 3, 1) .> DISTINCT()
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"1", "2"=t"2", "3"=t"3"}
===

### name: rel.distinct.strings
--- source
LIST("a", "b", "a") .> DISTINCT()
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"a", "2"=t"b"}
===

### name: rel.distinct.records
--- source
LIST(RECORD("k", 1), RECORD("k", 2), RECORD("k", 1)) .> DISTINCT()
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"k"=t"1"}, "2"=-{"k"=t"2"}}
===

### name: rel.distinct.null
--- source
DISTINCT(NULL)
--- expect
none
===

### name: rel.distinct.nested-lists
--- note
Identity of two lists is element by element (§3.4). One host compared the
lengths before it had bound them and crashed; four already answered.
--- source
LIST(LIST(1, 2), LIST(1, 2), LIST(1, 3)) .> DEDUPE()
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"1", "2"=t"2"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"1", "2"=t"3"}}
===

